For a stock at $30.65, I'll estimate typical daily volatility. TSCO historically has had annualized volatility around 25-30%. At $30.65, daily vol ≈ 30.65 × 0.27 / √252 ≈ $0.52/day.

For the confidence intervals:
- 1-day: ~1.645 × $0.52 ≈ ±$0.86
- 1-week (5 days): ~1.645 × $0.52 × √5 ≈ ±$1.91
- 1-month (~22 days): ~1.645 × $0.52 × √22 ≈ ±$4.01

Point estimates: slight upward drift assumed (small positive expected return).

